A||N||5||DaveT||2.5 engine removal?||||5||
Z||000000||DaveT||04-12-2000||12:23 AM||||I just purchased a 84'se with a 2.5 4 speed,<BR>cheap because of a bad rod knock.This is my first fiero,I have been researching replacing<BR>the engine,which i can do myself,but which is<BR>the easier way of doing it?can it be removed<BR>from the top?Or is it better to drop the whole assembly out the bottom?I have not got access to a hoist,but can get engine lift(cherry picker).<BR>help!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||wkayl||04-12-2000||12:48 AM||||I put a landscaping timber across the rafters in my garage.  I then removed the rear bumper to get access to metal frame of the car.  I put the car on jackstands with the rear wheels removed and unhooked the brake lines and left the rear struts (I think that is what you call them) in the car, just umbolting them from from where the calipers bolt on.  I unhooked all electrical connections (easy to rehook as they all have different connectors.  I used a chain hoist to lift the car up after removing the 4 carrige bolts.  I made a dolly out of 2x4's with casters.  It was easier to reinstall than to remove.  I didn't lift the entire car, just the body after engine was unbolted.  I think 2 people could have lifted it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||04-12-2000||01:50 AM||||I also remove the cradle from underneath.  You can leave the wire harness hooked to the engine by unplugging the large connector at the firewall and unplugging the fuel injection harness at the computer and feeding it back through the hole in the firewall.  I like to unbolt the calipers and hang them with coat hangar wire in the wheel wells.  I remove both struts as a complete assembly with the hubs attatched. This helps preserve the wheel alignment.  I use a piece of 2x6 lumber placed under the body just forward of the front cradle bolts and lower the car with a floor jack so that the cradle is resting on a dolly. ***Make sure the 2x6 board is long enough to span the entire width of the car***<BR>After removing the cradle bolts, jack up the body with the floor jack and 2x6.  A 22 inch lift on the jack should give you enough room to roll the engine on the dolly out from under the car.  It sounds a lot harder than it is.  The last time it took about an hour or so to remove the engine.  The main thing is to work carefully and safely!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-12-2000||03:53 AM||||As you seem to be gearing up for taking the engine out through the top, the 4 cyl is way easier than the 6.  You might want to get the alternator out and disconnect the AC compressor and secure it to the firewall so that you don't have to recharge it. The engine as you will see is only held on to by the torque strut (The dogbone thing on top) and the engine mount below. The tranny can remain hooked up.  Break out the 13 and 15 mm sockets as well as the 18 mm for the tranny bolts. There is just enough room for the engine to move forward and clear of the tranny. Have fun and good luck!<P>PS One thing that we learned was that on 4 cyl the lifter inspection plate must be well sealed. If it isn't oil can drip out and run along the bottom only to drip deceivingly from between the block and the tranny. This is especially easy if the block is painted black. I offer this to you so that you don't go back and tear the engine/tranny apart only to find an easy fix!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-12-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||007DOUG||04-12-2000||05:45 PM||||Visit my webpage <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse</A>  <P>Click on the Links page. On this page you will find various picture series of engine swaps and t-top installs. <P>You will find the 2.5 removal through the top series interesting. I took pics, and tried to explain each step in detail.<P> Its a brief picture series, and I hope it gives you an idea about what to do. I know I'll never take another 4cyl out the bottom again. Its much faster through the top.<P>Hope this helps, Doug||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaveT||04-12-2000||08:41 PM||||hey guys thanks!<BR>The info is awesome!<BR>Now i just need to find a decent engine.<BR>Thanks again.<BR>Dave<P> ||||reg||7
